[25.082493, "o", "OpenAI Codex v0.49.0 (research preview)\r\n--------\r\n\u001b[1mworkdir:\u001b[0m /app\r\n\u001b[1mmodel:\u001b[0m gpt-5\r\n\u001b[1mprovider:\u001b[0m openai\r\n\u001b[1mapproval:\u001b[0m never\r\n\u001b[1msandbox:\u001b[0m danger-full-access\r\n\u001b[1mreasoning effort:\u001b[0m none\r\n\u001b[1mreasoning summaries:\u001b[0m auto\r\n\u001b[1msession id:\u001b[0m 019a18cd-4268-7fd2-acfd-482ba64304c9\r\n--------\r\n\u001b[36muser\u001b[0m\r\nCreate an interactive fidget spinner visualization application at /app/fidget_spinner.py using Python's turtle graphics library. The application must match the following exact specifications.\r\n\r\nGlobal State and Configuration:\r\n- Create a state dictionary with 'turn' key initialized to 0\r\n- Create a colors list with exactly these colors in order: red, green, blue, yellow, purple\r\n- Define these configuration constants:\r\n  * ARMS_COUNT = 5\r\n  * ARM_LENGTH = 150\r\n  * ARM_WIDTH = 25\r\n  * OUTER_BORDER_DIAMETER = 140\r\n  * OUTER_INNER_DIAMETER = 120\r\n  * CENTER_BORDER_DIAMETER = 80\r\n  * CENTER_INNER_DIAMETER = 60\r\n\r\nRequired Functions:\r\n\r\n1. spinner() function:\r\n   - Clear the screen at "]
[25.082602, "o", "the start of each frame using clear()\r\n   - Calculate rotation angle from state['turn'] divided by 10\r\n   - Apply rotation using right(angle)\r\n   - Draw in three distinct layers:\r\n     a. Layer 1 - Arms: Draw 5 connecting arms from center, each ARM_LENGTH pixels long, width ARM_WIDTH, darkblue color, evenly spaced at 72 degree intervals\r\n     b. Layer 2 - Outer Bearings: At end of each arm, draw bearing with darkblue border (OUTER_BORDER_DIAMETER) and colored inner circle (OUTER_INNER_DIAMETER) using colors from list\r\n     c. Layer 3 - Center Hub: At origin, draw center with darkblue border (CENTER_BORDER_DIAMETER) and gray inner circle (CENTER_INNER_DIAMETER)\r\n   - Call update() after drawing\r\n\r\n2. animate() function:\r\n   - If state['turn'] is greater than 0, decrease it by 1\r\n   - Call spinner() to redraw\r\n   - Schedule next frame using ontimer(animate, 20) for 20 millisecond delay\r\n\r\n3. flick() function:\r\n   - Add 10 to state['turn']\r\n\r\nMain Setup:\r\n- Window: 600x600 pixels at position (370, 0) using setup"]
[25.082641, "o", "(600, 600, 370, 0)\r\n- Hide turtle cursor with hideturtle()\r\n- Turn off automatic updates with tracer(False)\r\n- Background color: lightblue using bgcolor('lightblue')\r\n- Enable event listening with listen()\r\n- Bind spacebar to flick function using onkey(flick, 'space')\r\n- Start animation loop by calling animate()\r\n- Keep window open with done()\r\n\r\nSuccess Criteria:\r\n- File exists at /app/fidget_spinner.py\r\n- File contains valid Python syntax\r\n- All required functions (spinner, animate, flick) are defined\r\n- State dictionary exists with 'turn' key\r\n- Colors list contains the five colors in correct order\r\n- All configuration constants are defined with correct values\r\n- Flick function adds exactly 10 to state['turn']\r\n- Animate function decreases state['turn'] by 1 when greater than 0\r\n- Window is configured with correct dimensions\r\n- Event binding connects spacebar to flick function\r\n- Animation uses 20 millisecond timing\r\n"]
